OpenLiteSpeed 1.9.3 — add lsadm to the server's group only as root, only if lsadm exists.

configServerBasics() runs, on EVERY start and every config test,
  macOS:  dseditgroup -o edit -a lsadm -t user <group>
  Linux:  usermod -a -G <group> lsadm
  BSD:    pw usermod lsadm -G <group>
with no check of who is running it. As an ordinary user (rexenv never runs
OpenLiteSpeed as root) it always fails, and on macOS dseditgroup prints
"Username and password must be provided." into the server's stdout — found by the
build gate, 4 Oct 2026. As root it edits the host's group database at every start.
Guarded on getuid() == 0 and getpwnam("lsadm") — the same two conditions
fixConfDirsPermission() a few lines below already requires. Upstreamable.

diff --git a/src/main/httpserver.cpp b/src/main/httpserver.cpp
index b5c37db..6fb8556 100644
--- a/src/main/httpserver.cpp
+++ b/src/main/httpserver.cpp
@@ -4185,7 +4185,12 @@ int HttpServerImpl::configServerBasics(int reconfig, const XmlNode *pRoot)
 #if defined(macintosh) || defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__APPLE_CC__)
         snprintf(syscmd, 1024, "dseditgroup -o edit -a lsadm -t user %s", MainServerConfigObj.getGroup());
 #endif
-        if (*syscmd)
+        /* Only root can add a user to a group, and only a host with the lsadm
+         * user has one to add. Unguarded, every start by an ordinary user ran
+         * dseditgroup/usermod, failed, and printed "Username and password must
+         * be provided." (macOS) into stdout — and as root it edits the system's
+         * group database on every start. */
+        if (*syscmd && getuid() == 0 && getpwnam("lsadm") != NULL)
             ::system(syscmd);
 
         return 0;
